# =============================================================================
# DATABASE CONFIGURATION
# =============================================================================
# Uncomment ONE of the following DATABASE_URL options:

# --- SQLite (default for local development — no setup needed) ---
# DATABASE_URL=sqlite:///resource_tracker.db

# --- MS SQL Server (SQL Authentication) ---
# DATABASE_URL=mssql+pyodbc://username:password@server:1433/database_name?driver=ODBC+Driver+18+for+SQL+Server&TrustServerCertificate=yes

# --- MS SQL Server (Windows Authentication) ---
# DATABASE_URL=mssql+pyodbc://server/database_name?driver=ODBC+Driver+18+for+SQL+Server&Trusted_Connection=yes

# --- Azure SQL Database ---
# DATABASE_URL=mssql+pyodbc://username:password@myserver.database.windows.net:1433/database_name?driver=ODBC+Driver+18+for+SQL+Server&Encrypt=yes&TrustServerCertificate=no

# =============================================================================
# NOTES:
# - Install ODBC Driver 18 for SQL Server: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/sql/connect/odbc/download-odbc-driver-for-sql-server
# - If using ODBC Driver 17, change "ODBC+Driver+18+for+SQL+Server" to "ODBC+Driver+17+for+SQL+Server"
# - Special characters in password must be URL-encoded (e.g., @ = %40, # = %23)
# - For Azure, ensure firewall rules allow your IP
# =============================================================================
